 "final_passage": "Marrowfield-ASR meets the pre-specified robustness criterion of a WER increase of at most 1.5 absolute points at all tested noise levels, with increases of 0.3, 0.9, and 1.3 points at 20, 10, and 5 dB SNR, respectively. Marrowfield-ASR also shows smaller WER increases under noise than Ostrander-CTC at every tested SNR (0.3 vs 1.1 points at 20 dB, 0.9 vs 3.2 at 10 dB, and 1.3 vs 6.6 at 5 dB). On the original clean recordings, Marrowfield-ASR achieves a lower WER (5.8%) than both Ostrander-CTC (6.4%) and Pellucid-RNNT (6.1%), though no statistical tests are reported for any of these comparisons.",
